I see. Being generally kind doesn’t mean you’re incapable of aggression, sharpness, spite, or enjoying the occasional hard edge.

The useful distinction is:

\text{capacity for meanness} \neq \text{obligation to express it}

Sometimes that streak is protective—boundary setting, competitive intensity, refusing to be pushed around. Sometimes it’s just an itch that feels satisfying to scratch and leaves damage afterward.

The trick is being able to use the edge without letting the edge choose the target.

Nice with teeth is different from harmless.